(24664, 'The Beginning of a New Mine-Shaft',
 'Particularly rich finding of crystal lode mining is the reason this tunnel has been recently cut. Somewhat more tidy than the exploited sections, there are relatively few scraps in the rock and few excavations. However, judging by the amount of work here, this will quickly change. Only the most sturdiest and strongest of the miners work here, because they were able to surpress the weaker ones and keep them at bay. The tunnel turns here, wrapping around indestructible rock.'),
(24665, 'At the Turn near the Entrance to the New Mine-Shaft',
 'Particularly rich finding of crystal lode mining is the reason this tunnel has been recently cut. Somewhat more tidy than the exploited sections, there are relatively few scraps in the rock and few excavations. However, judging by the amount of work here, this will quickly change. Only the most sturdiest and strongest of the miners work here, because they were able to surpress the weaker ones and keep them at bay. The tunnel turns here, wrapping around indestructible rock.'),
(24666, 'The End of a New Mine-Shaft',
 'The crystal is as strongly present in this cave as it is through the rest of the region. The only reason the miners did not expand here is because they are too busy exploiting the shafts to the east of here. The rock is particularly soft here and it looks as if this spot will be very promising indeed. North and south, you notice expansive emptiness, with strange sounds echoing through it.'),
(24667, 'Underground Grotto',
 'You enter a small, dark cavern, with water dripping from the ceiling. The crystal veins are apparantly non-existant here, with only the soft rock making up the walls. The strange echoing of this cavern is strong here, making you uneasy.'),
(24668, 'Rough Natural Cavern',
 'The quantity of crystal here is amazing, as even the most miniscule amount of light is reflected ten-fold among the crystals. The rock here is still quite soft, making this cavern an amazing find. Sound echoes oddly here, however, giving this cavern an eerie feel, almost unnatural.'),
