(24700, 'Inside an Old, Exploited Excavation',
 'Piles of debris and broken mining equipment are strewn across the uneven floor of this excavation. Where once there was a plethora of crystal, now only little veins remain. Just as the excavation has lost its glamour, so did the miners that work it now: old and sturdy, they none the less lack the strength of the younger miners.'),
(24701, 'Atop the Portcullis',
 'The quality of the air is somewhat better here. This is likely due to the fact that this point dominates the rest of the cave system visible to you by its height. Still, odours from below you drift up slowly of their own accord, and you are soon reminded of the filth beneath you. You can continue to walk along the fortified wall either east or west.'),
(24702, 'Within a Wide Grotto',
 'The tall walls of grotto disappear into the darkness above you. An unexpected ending to the miners'' tunnel, there is an uneasy feeling about this place that you just can''t quite name yet. Crude voices can be heard clamoring to the north.'),
(24703, 'Along the Southern Wall',
 'This is the southern wall surrounding the natural valley extending northwards. The wall is crude, tall and wide enough for a little group to traverse easily. It appears to have been created when a lava eruption from times gone by finally solidified.'),
(24704, 'Along the Southern Wall',
 'This is the southern wall surrounding the natural valley extending northwards. The wall is crude, tall and wide enough for a little group to traverse easily. It appears to have been created when a lava eruption from times gone by finally solidified.'),
(24705, 'At the South-Western Turret',
 'One of the sites that have seen the most of construction, this turret is nothing more than a few rough wooden beams put together to support a few guards as they oversee the cave. The view from this point is rather good, and the ugliness of a hobgoblin dwelling reveals itself in all of its pitifulness.'),
(24706, 'At the South-Western Turret',
 'One of the sites that have seen the most of construction, this turret is nothing more than a few rough wooden beams put together to support a few guards as they oversee the cave. The view from this point is rather good, and the ugliness of a hobgoblin dwelling reveals itself in all of its pitifulness.'),
(24707, 'At the South-Western Turren',
 'One of the sites that have seen the most of construction, this turret is nothing more than a few rough wooden beams put together to support a few guards as they oversee the cave. The view from this point is rather good, and the ugliness of a hobgoblin dwelling reveals itself in all of its pitifulness.'),
(24708, 'Along the Western Wall',
 'You are standing at the western side of a natural wall surrounding a valley to the west. You can spot a commotion all across valley, as it hobgoblins move about in scores. To your west, there is nothing but darkness.'),
(24709, 'Along the Western Wall',
 'You are standing at the western side of a natural wall surrounding a valley to the west. You can spot a commotion all across valley, as it hobgoblins move about in scores. To your west, there is nothing but darkness.'),
(24710, 'At the North-Western Turret',
 'Unlike the southern turrets, this one is constructed from a few rough-hewn blocks of stone, joined together by mortar. The reason for this is the scarcitiy of the wood underground. Never the less, there is enough room for two guards to comfortably observe the activites at the valley floor.'),
(24711, 'At the North-Western Turret',
 'Unlike the southern turrets, this one is constructed from a few rough-hewn blocks of stone, joined together by mortar. The reason for this is the scarcitiy of the wood underground. Never the less, there is enough room for two guards to comfortably observe the activites at the valley floor.'),
(24712, 'At the North-Western Turret',
 'Unlike the southern turrets, this one is constructed from a few rough-hewn blocks of stone, joined together by mortar. The reason for this is the scarcitiy of the wood underground. Never the less, there is enough room for two guards to comfortably observe the activites at the valley floor.'),
(24713, 'Where the Wall Meets the Ridge',
 'All the attempts of hobgoblins at further constructing the battlements on the wall stop here. Ill-executed masonary creations have been battered, likely in frustration. However, they had little reason to worry: nothing can climb the ridge extending eastwards from you without being noticed by guards.'),
(24714, 'Along the Northern Ridge',
 'Secure in the natural defenses of the northern ridge, this section of the wall is untouched by the goblins. The northern ridge here is immense, and in full view of the entire stronghold. To your north is only darkness beyond the ridge, and you can continue along the wall to the east and west.'),
(24715, 'Along the Northern Ridge',
 'Secure in the natural defenses of the northern ridge, this section of the wall is untouched by the goblins. The northern ridge here is immense, and in full view of the entire stronghold. To your north is only darkness beyond the ridge, and you can continue along the wall to the east and west.'),
(24716, 'Inside the Portcullis',
 'Massive iron portcullis is behind you to the south. You can feel the pungent odor of urine around you. It is augmented by the warm, moist atmosphere of the caves, making you quite nauseous. The chamber itself looks dank and oppresive, with pieces of garbage strewn across the uneven floor. You spot a narrow staircase which leads upwards. Before you, towards the north, a small dweling sprawls in the natural valley.'),
(24717, 'Along the Southern Wall',
 'This is the southern wall surrounding the natural valley extending northwards. The wall is crude, tall and wide enough for a little group to traverse easily. It appears to have been created when a lava eruption from times gone by finally solidified.'),
