(24727, 'Where the Wall Meets the Ridge',
 'All the attempts of hobgoblins at further constructing the battlements on the wall stop here. Ill-executed masonary creations have been battered, likely in frustration. However, they had little reason to worry: nothing can climb the ridge extending westwards from you without being noticed by guards.'),
(24728, 'The Main Chamber of the Hut',
 'The most opulent room in the entire mine system, the goblin who resides here must obviously be the local king. Every possible space is covered in goblin treasure, and some of it actually has some real value. Cluttered beyond belief, both the appearance and the stench make it obvious the king has little care to have this room cleaned. As you take this in, you realize the owner of these valuables is probably rather jealous of his possessions, and would not leave them for long.'),
(24729, 'Along the Northern Ridge',
 'Secure in the natural defenses of the northern ridge, this section of the wall is untouched by the goblins. The northern ridge here is immense, and in full view of the entire stronghold. To your north is only darkness beyond the ridge, and you can continue along the wall to the east and west.'),
(24730, 'On the Main Path through the Stronghold',
 'The scattered debris lays all around you. Heaps and heaps of the discarded necessities of the life: torn, dried skins, broken weapons and piles of excretements are all around you. It is obvious that the denizens of this stronghold did not attribute too much importance to the hygiene. However, one thing that makes this region stand out from the rest of the fortress is that the debris has been pushed aside, so as to make a clear path.'),
(24731, 'On the Main Path through the Stronghold',
 'The scattered debris lays all around you. Heaps and heaps of the discarded necessities of the life: torn, dried skins, broken weapons and piles of excretements are all around you. It is obvious that the denizens of this stronghold did not attribute too much importance to the hygiene. However, one thing that makes this region stand out from the rest of the fortress is that the debris has been pushed aside, so as to make a clear path.'),
(24732, 'The End of the Main Path through Stronghold',
 'The piles of debris stocked up against either side of the path cease to exist here. Rather, the chaotic arrangement of the garbage form a uniform mass once again before your eyes. The stench of the garbage is accentuated by the strong scent of unwashed goblin bodies.'),
(24733, 'Under the Northern Wall',
 'The oppresive, black wall rises before your eyes, disappearing in the darkness of the caverns high above. Upon closer inspection, it becomes apparent that the wall is not the product of the goblins. Rather, they seem to have taken advantage of the natural formation of the rocks that already existed here.'),
(24734, 'Under the Southern Wall',
 'The oppresive, black wall rises before your eyes, disappearing in the darkness of the caverns high above. Upon closer inspection, it becomes apparent that the wall is not the product of the goblins. Rather, they seem to have taken advantage of the natural formation of the rocks that already existed here.'),
(24735, 'Under the Southern Wall',
 'The oppresive, black wall rises before your eyes, disappearing in the darkness of the caverns high above. Upon closer inspection, it becomes apparent that the wall is not the product of the goblins. Rather, they seem to have taken advantage of the natural formation of the rocks that already existed here.'),
(24736, 'Under the South-Western Turret',
 'The oppresive, black wall rises before your eyes, disappearing in the darkness of the caverns high above. Upon closer inspection, it becomes apparent that the wall is not the product of the goblins. Rather, they seem to have taken advantage of the natural formation of the rocks that already existed here. Above you, several goblins can be heard chittering in the darkness.'),
(24737, 'In the Stronghold',
 'The visible signs of rampant carelesness are laid out in front of your eyes. Piles of debris have been chaotically formed all over the perimiter of the stronghold. Where there is no debris, the stone has been charred by what must have been a considerable fire. The stench of goblin horde hovers in the air, as the stronghold stretches all around you.'),
