(24758, 'The Forechamber of the Hut',
 'The first chamber of the hut is as opulent, by goblin standards, as the entrance. This is the central intersection of the hut, with the doorways leading west and north. The walls are decorated with crude pictures, while the floor has a few dark stains across it. There only air that comes in or out of the chamber comes from the entrance to the south of you. Thus it is not surprising that the stench is rather strong.'),
(24759, 'Under the Northern Wall',
 'The oppresive, black wall rises before your eyes, disappearing in the darkness of the caverns high above. Upon closer inspection, it becomes apparent that the wall is not the product of the goblins. Rather, they seem to have taken advantage of the natural formation of the rocks that already existed here.'),
