(24773, 'The Chamber of Fire',
 'Small chamber that branches off from the forechamber of the hut is strangely devoid of any excessive ornaments which grace the rest of this hut. Ascetic and minimalistic, it seems that someone has taken a great deal of effort to keep the place uncluttered by trinkets. The ceiling of this chamber is lower than the rest of the hut. You notice that it is covered in soot, as well as all the walls of the chamber.')
